---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Manual Setup — Resolvd" description="Step-by-step Resolvd setup with branching choices for each component.">
  <section class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 pt-16 pb-10">
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight">Manual Setup</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-fg-muted)] max-w-2xl">
        Choose-your-own-adventure. Each step has options — pick what fits your stack.
        Prefer a click-through? <a href="/install/" class="text-[var(--color-brand)] hover:underline">Use the wizard</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-12 space-y-8">

      <!-- Step 0 -->
      <article class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-surface)] p-6">
        <header class="flex items-baseline gap-3">
          <span class="text-[var(--color-brand)] font-mono text-sm">00</span>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Prerequisites</h2>
        </header>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm text-[var(--color-fg-muted)] list-disc list-inside">
          <li>Linux host (any distro). 1 vCPU, 1 GB RAM, 10 GB disk minimum.</li>
          <li>A DNS A/AAAA record pointing at your host (or a Cloudflare Tunnel).</li>
          <li>Docker 24+ and Docker Compose plugin v2.</li>
          <li>Git.</li>
        </ul>
        <pre class="code-block mt-4"><span class="c"># Ubuntu/Debian one-liner</span>
<span class="k">curl</span> -fsSL https://get.docker.com | sh
<span class="k">sudo</span> usermod -aG docker $USER  <span class="c"># log out / in after</span></pre>
      </article>

      <!-- Step 1 -->
      <article class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-surface)] p-6">
        <header class="flex items-baseline gap-3">
          <span class="text-[var(--color-brand)] font-mono text-sm">01</span>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Clone the source</h2>
        </header>
        <pre class="code-block mt-4"><span class="k">git</span> clone https://github.com/joshhearne/resolvd.git
<span class="k">cd</span> resolvd</pre>
      </article>

      <!-- Step 2 -->
      <article class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-surface)] p-6">
        <header class="flex items-baseline gap-3">
          <span class="text-[var(--color-brand)] font-mono text-sm">02</span>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Generate secrets</h2>
        </header>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-[var(--color-fg-muted)]">You need two: a Postgres password and a session secret. Both 32+ chars.</p>
        <pre class="code-block mt-4"><span class="k">openssl</span> rand -hex 32  <span class="c"># SESSION_SECRET</span>
<span class="k">openssl</span> rand -base64 32  <span class="c"># POSTGRES_PASSWORD</span></pre>
      </article>

      <!-- Step 3 -->
      <article class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-surface)] p-6">
        <header class="flex items-baseline gap-3">
          <span class="text-[var(--color-brand)] font-mono text-sm">03</span>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Pick your auth providers</h2>
        </header>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-[var(--color-fg-muted)]">You can mix and match. Local always works as a fallback.</p>

        <details class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-surface-2)]">
          <summary class="flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-3 hover:bg-[var(--color-bg)] rounded-lg">
            <span class="chev text-[var(--color-brand)]">▸</span>
            <span class="font-medium">Option A — Local accounts only</span>
            <span class="ml-auto text-xs text-[var(--color-fg-dim)]">Easiest</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-4 pb-4 pt-2 text-sm text-[var(--color-fg-muted)] space-y-2">
            <p>Nothing to configure. Sign up at <code>/signup</code> after first boot — first account becomes Admin.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="mt-2 rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-surface-2)]">
          <summary class="flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-3 hover:bg-[var(--color-bg)] rounded-lg">
            <span class="chev text-[var(--color-brand)]">▸</span>
            <span class="font-medium">Option B — Microsoft Entra ID</span>
            <span class="ml-auto text-xs text-[var(--color-fg-dim)]">Workspace SSO</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-4 pb-4 pt-2 text-sm text-[var(--color-fg-muted)] space-y-3">
            <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-1.5">
              <li>Go to <a href="https://entra.microsoft.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-[var(--color-brand)] hover:underline">Entra admin center</a> → App registrations → New.</li>
              <li>Redirect URI (Web): <code>https://yourdomain.com/auth/callback</code></li>
              <li>API permissions: <code>User.Read</code>, optionally <code>Mail.Send</code> for email.</li>
              <li>Certificates &amp; secrets → New client secret. Copy it now.</li>
              <li>Drop these into your <code>.env</code>:</li>
            </ol>
            <pre class="code-block" is:raw>AZURE_TENANT_ID=...
AZURE_CLIENT_ID=...
AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET=...
AZURE_REDIRECT_URI=https://yourdomain.com/auth/callback
AZURE_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://yourdomain.com</pre>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="mt-2 rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-surface-2)]">
          <summary class="flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-3 hover:bg-[var(--color-bg)] rounded-lg">
            <span class="chev text-[var(--color-brand)]">▸</span>
            <span class="font-medium">Option C — Google OAuth</span>
            <span class="ml-auto text-xs text-[var(--color-fg-dim)]">Workspace or consumer</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-4 pb-4 pt-2 text-sm text-[var(--color-fg-muted)] space-y-3">
            <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-1.5">
              <li>Open <a href="https://console.cloud.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-[var(--color-brand)] hover:underline">Google Cloud Console</a> → APIs &amp; Services → Credentials.</li>
              <li>Create OAuth client ID → Web application.</li>
              <li>Authorized redirect URI: <code>https://yourdomain.com/auth/google/callback</code></li>
              <li>Copy client ID and secret into <code>.env</code>:</li>
            </ol>
            <pre class="code-block" is:raw>GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=...
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=...
GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=https://yourdomain.com/auth/google/callback</pre>
          </div>
        </details>
      </article>

      <!-- Step 4 -->
      <article class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-surface)] p-6">
        <header class="flex items-baseline gap-3">
          <span class="text-[var(--color-brand)] font-mono text-sm">04</span>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Pick your email backend</h2>
        </header>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-[var(--color-fg-muted)]">Optional. Skip entirely if you don't want notifications.</p>

        <details class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-surface-2)]">
          <summary class="flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-3 hover:bg-[var(--color-bg)]"><span class="chev text-[var(--color-brand)]">▸</span><span class="font-medium">Microsoft Graph</span><span class="ml-auto text-xs text-[var(--color-fg-dim)]">Reuses Entra app</span></summary>
          <div class="px-4 pb-4 pt-2 text-sm text-[var(--color-fg-muted)] space-y-2">
            <p>Add <code>Mail.Send</code> application permission to your Entra app, then grant admin consent.</p>
            <pre class="code-block" is:raw>MAIL_BACKEND=graph
MAIL_FROM=noreply@yourdomain.com</pre>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="mt-2 rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-surface-2)]">
          <summary class="flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-3 hover:bg-[var(--color-bg)]"><span class="chev text-[var(--color-brand)]">▸</span><span class="font-medium">Gmail API</span><span class="ml-auto text-xs text-[var(--color-fg-dim)]">Reuses Google app</span></summary>
          <div class="px-4 pb-4 pt-2 text-sm text-[var(--color-fg-muted)] space-y-2">
            <p>Enable Gmail API in your Google Cloud project. Add <code>gmail.send</code> scope.</p>
            <pre class="code-block" is:raw>MAIL_BACKEND=gmail
MAIL_FROM=noreply@yourdomain.com</pre>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="mt-2 rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-surface-2)]">
          <summary class="flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-3 hover:bg-[var(--color-bg)]"><span class="chev text-[var(--color-brand)]">▸</span><span class="font-medium">SMTP</span><span class="ml-auto text-xs text-[var(--color-fg-dim)]">Postmark, SendGrid, etc.</span></summary>
          <div class="px-4 pb-4 pt-2 text-sm text-[var(--color-fg-muted)] space-y-2">
            <pre class="code-block" is:raw>MAIL_BACKEND=smtp
MAIL_FROM=noreply@yourdomain.com
SMTP_HOST=smtp.postmarkapp.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=...
SMTP_PASSWORD=...</pre>
          </div>
        </details>
      </article>

      <!-- Step 5 -->
      <article class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-surface)] p-6">
        <header class="flex items-baseline gap-3">
          <span class="text-[var(--color-brand)] font-mono text-sm">05</span>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Bring up the stack</h2>
        </header>
        <pre class="code-block mt-4"><span class="k">cp</span> .env.example .env  <span class="c"># paste in everything from steps 2–4</span>
<span class="k">mkdir</span> -p data/uploads
<span class="k">docker</span> compose up -d --build
<span class="k">docker</span> compose logs -f</pre>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-[var(--color-fg-muted)]">Stack now bound to <code>127.0.0.1:8090</code>. Not reachable externally yet.</p>
      </article>

      <!-- Step 6 -->
      <article class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-surface)] p-6">
        <header class="flex items-baseline gap-3">
          <span class="text-[var(--color-brand)] font-mono text-sm">06</span>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Pick your reverse proxy</h2>
        </header>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-[var(--color-fg-muted)]">Pick one. All terminate TLS and forward to <code>127.0.0.1:8090</code>.</p>

        <details class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-surface-2)]" open>
          <summary class="flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-3 hover:bg-[var(--color-bg)]"><span class="chev text-[var(--color-brand)]">▸</span><span class="font-medium">Caddy</span><span class="ml-auto text-xs text-[var(--color-fg-dim)]">Auto-TLS, easiest</span></summary>
          <div class="px-4 pb-4 pt-2 text-sm text-[var(--color-fg-muted)] space-y-2">
            <pre class="code-block" is:raw><span class="c"># /etc/caddy/Caddyfile</span>
yourdomain.com {
    reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8090
    request_body { max_size 50MB }
}</pre>
            <pre class="code-block" is:raw><span class="k">sudo</span> systemctl reload caddy</pre>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="mt-2 rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-surface-2)]">
          <summary class="flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-3 hover:bg-[var(--color-bg)]"><span class="chev text-[var(--color-brand)]">▸</span><span class="font-medium">nginx + Certbot</span><span class="ml-auto text-xs text-[var(--color-fg-dim)]">Most familiar</span></summary>
          <div class="px-4 pb-4 pt-2 text-sm text-[var(--color-fg-muted)] space-y-2">
            <pre class="code-block" is:raw><span class="c"># /etc/nginx/sites-available/resolvd</span>
server {
    listen 80;
    server_name yourdomain.com;

    client_max_body_size 50M;
    location / {
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8090;
        proxy_set_header Host              $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP         $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For   $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    }
}</pre>
            <pre class="code-block" is:raw><span class="k">sudo</span> ln -s /etc/nginx/sites-available/resolvd /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/
<span class="k">sudo</span> nginx -t && sudo systemctl reload nginx
<span class="k">sudo</span> certbot --nginx -d yourdomain.com</pre>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="mt-2 rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-surface-2)]">
          <summary class="flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-3 hover:bg-[var(--color-bg)]"><span class="chev text-[var(--color-brand)]">▸</span><span class="font-medium">Cloudflare Tunnel</span><span class="ml-auto text-xs text-[var(--color-fg-dim)]">No open ports</span></summary>
          <div class="px-4 pb-4 pt-2 text-sm text-[var(--color-fg-muted)] space-y-2">
            <pre class="code-block" is:raw><span class="k">cloudflared</span> tunnel login
<span class="k">cloudflared</span> tunnel create resolvd
<span class="k">cloudflared</span> tunnel route dns resolvd yourdomain.com</pre>
            <p>Edit <code>~/.cloudflared/config.yml</code>:</p>
            <pre class="code-block" is:raw>tunnel: &lt;tunnel-uuid&gt;
credentials-file: ~/.cloudflared/&lt;uuid&gt;.json
ingress:
  - hostname: yourdomain.com
    service: http://127.0.0.1:8090
  - service: http_status:404</pre>
            <pre class="code-block" is:raw><span class="k">cloudflared</span> service install</pre>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="mt-2 rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-surface-2)]">
          <summary class="flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-3 hover:bg-[var(--color-bg)]"><span class="chev text-[var(--color-brand)]">▸</span><span class="font-medium">Traefik</span><span class="ml-auto text-xs text-[var(--color-fg-dim)]">Container-native</span></summary>
          <div class="px-4 pb-4 pt-2 text-sm text-[var(--color-fg-muted)] space-y-2">
            <p>Add labels to the <code>nginx</code> service in <code>docker-compose.yml</code> and put it on your Traefik network:</p>
            <pre class="code-block" is:raw>labels:
  - "traefik.enable=true"
  - "traefik.http.routers.resolvd.rule=Host(`yourdomain.com`)"
  - "traefik.http.routers.resolvd.entrypoints=websecure"
  - "traefik.http.routers.resolvd.tls.certresolver=letsencrypt"
  - "traefik.http.services.resolvd.loadbalancer.server.port=80"</pre>
          </div>
        </details>
      </article>

      <!-- Step 7 -->
      <article class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-surface)] p-6">
        <header class="flex items-baseline gap-3">
          <span class="text-[var(--color-brand)] font-mono text-sm">07</span>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">First-run setup</h2>
        </header>
        <ol class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm text-[var(--color-fg-muted)] list-decimal list-inside">
          <li>Visit <code>https://yourdomain.com</code>.</li>
          <li>Sign up — first account becomes Admin automatically.</li>
          <li>Admin → Authentication: enable Entra/Google if you configured them.</li>
          <li>Admin → Branding: upload logo, set color, change site name.</li>
          <li>Admin → Users: invite your team, set roles.</li>
          <li>Create your first project. Done.</li>
        </ol>
      </article>

      <!-- Backups -->
      <article class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-surface)] p-6">
        <header class="flex items-baseline gap-3">
          <span class="text-[var(--color-brand)] font-mono text-sm">08</span>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Backups</h2>
        </header>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-[var(--color-fg-muted)]">Two things to back up: the Postgres volume and the uploads volume.</p>
        <pre class="code-block mt-4"><span class="c"># Postgres dump (run on the host)</span>
<span class="k">docker</span> exec resolvd-postgres pg_dump -U mot_issues mot_issues \
  | gzip > backup-$(date +%F).sql.gz

<span class="c"># Uploads (rsync or tar the volume)</span>
<span class="k">docker</span> run --rm -v resolvd_uploads-data:/src -v $(pwd):/dst \
  alpine tar czf /dst/uploads-$(date +%F).tar.gz -C /src .</pre>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-[var(--color-fg-muted)]">Cron both nightly. Ship to S3/B2/wherever.</p>
      </article>

      <div class="text-center pt-6">
        <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-fg-muted)]">Stuck? <a href="https://github.com/joshhearne/resolvd/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-[var(--color-brand)] hover:underline">Open an issue</a> on GitHub.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
